IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc5-logic`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, 1992 c. 4 -- part ssc5.
-- PART VIII, THE SOCIAL FUND (ss 138 to 140) and PART 8A, HEALTH IN PREGNANCY GRANT (ss 140A, 140B).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from legislation.gov.uk (point in time
-- 2026-07-08); it is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- Reading a result: JUST FALSE is the Act saying no in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md).
-- K3 (s 174, line 4342): in this file "the Administration Act" is the Social Security Administration Act 1992.
-- Every NOT is bracketed.  Payments out of the social fund are discretionary: the Act says what MAY be paid
-- and what the officer must have regard to, so a result of JUST TRUE here means "the Act allows it" or
-- "the Act requires it", as each function's name says, never "the applicant is owed it".

§ `Part VIII -- The social fund (ss 138-140)`

§§ `s 138 -- payments out of the social fund`

DECLARE `s 138(1) Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet maternity expenses`
    `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet funeral expenses`
    `s 138(1)(b) a community care grant`
    `s 138(1)(b) a crisis loan`
    `s 138(1)(b) a budgeting loan`
    `s 138(1) some other kind of payment`

-- A permission: "There may be made out of the social fund".  Paragraph (a) payments are of prescribed amounts in
-- prescribed circumstances; paragraph (b) payments are made in accordance with directions given or guidance issued.
-- src:2851 | (1) There may be made out of the social fund, in accordance with this Part of this Act—
-- src:2852 | (a) payments of prescribed amounts, whether in respect of prescribed items or otherwise, to meet, in prescribed circumstances, maternity expenses and funeral expenses; and
-- src:2853 | (b) payments by way of community care grant, crisis loan or budgeting loan to meet—
-- src:2854 | (i) other needs, and
-- src:2855 | (ii) in the case of payments by way of budgeting loan, those needs for which provision is made by paragraph (a),
-- src:2856 | in accordance with directions given or guidance issued by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 138(1) (src:2851-2856)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 138(1) Kind of payment`
      `the amount is a prescribed amount and the circumstances are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is in accordance with directions given or guidance issued by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(1) the payment may be made out of the social fund` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet maternity expenses` THEN
        IF `the amount is a prescribed amount and the circumstances are prescribed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "payments of prescribed amounts ... in prescribed circumstances"
    WHEN `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet funeral expenses` THEN
        IF `the amount is a prescribed amount and the circumstances are prescribed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "payments of prescribed amounts ... in prescribed circumstances"
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a community care grant` THEN
        IF `the payment is in accordance with directions given or guidance issued by the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with directions given or guidance issued by the Secretary of State"
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a crisis loan` THEN
        IF `the payment is in accordance with directions given or guidance issued by the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): same
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a budgeting loan` THEN
        IF `the payment is in accordance with directions given or guidance issued by the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): same
    WHEN `s 138(1) some other kind of payment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection lists the payments that may be made and does not say "only"

-- Heating payments in cold weather: a prescribed amount, to prescribed descriptions of persons, in prescribed
-- circumstances, for expenses that appear to the Secretary of State to have been or to be likely to be incurred.
-- src:2857 | (2) Payments may also be made out of that fund, in accordance with this Part of this Act, of a prescribed amount or a number of prescribed amounts to prescribed descriptions of persons, in prescribed circumstances to meet expenses for heating which appear to the Secretary of State to have been or to be likely to be incurred in cold weather.
@ref s 138(2) (src:2857)
GIVEN `the amount is a prescribed amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is of a prescribed description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expenses are for heating and appear to the Secretary of State to have been or to be likely to be incurred in cold weather` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(2) the heating payment may be made out of the social fund` MEANS
    IF     `the amount is a prescribed amount`
       AND `the person is of a prescribed description`
       AND `the circumstances are prescribed`
       AND `the expenses are for heating and appear to the Secretary of State to have been or to be likely to be incurred in cold weather`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of a prescribed amount ... to prescribed descriptions of persons, in prescribed circumstances to meet expenses for heating which appear to the Secretary of State"

-- The power in (1)(b) may be exercised by paying a third party.
-- src:2858 | (3) The power to make a payment out of the social fund such as is mentioned in subsection (1)(b) above may be exercised by making a payment to a third party with a view to the third party providing, or arranging for the provision of, goods or services for the applicant.
@ref s 138(3) (src:2858)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 138(1) Kind of payment`
      `the payment is made to a third party with a view to the third party providing, or arranging for the provision of, goods or services for the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(3) the payment may be made to a third party` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a community care grant` THEN
        IF `the payment is made to a third party with a view to the third party providing, or arranging for the provision of, goods or services for the applicant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with a view to the third party providing, or arranging for the provision of, goods or services for the applicant"
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a crisis loan` THEN
        IF `the payment is made to a third party with a view to the third party providing, or arranging for the provision of, goods or services for the applicant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): same
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a budgeting loan` THEN
        IF `the payment is made to a third party with a view to the third party providing, or arranging for the provision of, goods or services for the applicant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): same
    WHEN `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet maternity expenses` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such as is mentioned in subsection (1)(b)"
    WHEN `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet funeral expenses` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such as is mentioned in subsection (1)(b)"
    WHEN `s 138(1) some other kind of payment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such as is mentioned in subsection (1)(b)"

DECLARE `s 138(4) Defined term` IS ONE OF
    `s 138(4) prescribed`

-- src:2859 | (4) In this section “prescribed” means specified in or determined in accordance with regulations.
@ref s 138(4) (src:2859)
GIVEN term IS A `s 138(4) Defined term`
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 138(4) how the term is defined` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
        `what it points at or says` IS "specified in or determined in accordance with regulations"

-- In or as regards Scotland the section is read with three substitutions.
DECLARE `s 138(4A) Reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 138(4A)(a) the making of payments out of the social fund, in subsections (1)(a) and (2)`
    `s 138(4A)(b) the Secretary of State, in subsection (2)`
    `s 138(4A)(c) regulations, in subsection (4)`

-- src:2860 | (4A) This section has effect in or as regards Scotland as if—
-- src:2861 | (a) references in subsections (1)(a) and (2) to the making of payments out of the social fund were to the making of payments by the Scottish Ministers,
-- src:2862 | (b) the reference in subsection (2) to the Secretary of State were to the Scottish Ministers, and
-- src:2863 | (c) the reference in subsection (4) to regulations were to regulations made by the Scottish Ministers.
@ref s 138(4A) (src:2860-2863)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 138(4A) Reference`
      `the case is in or as regards Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 138(4A) the reference is read in Scotland as` MEANS
    IF `the case is in or as regards Scotland`
    THEN
        CONSIDER reference
        WHEN `s 138(4A)(a) the making of payments out of the social fund, in subsections (1)(a) and (2)` THEN JUST "the making of payments by the Scottish Ministers"
        WHEN `s 138(4A)(b) the Secretary of State, in subsection (2)` THEN JUST "the Scottish Ministers"
        WHEN `s 138(4A)(c) regulations, in subsection (4)` THEN JUST "regulations made by the Scottish Ministers"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section has effect in or as regards Scotland as if"

-- Regulations made by the Scottish Ministers under this section: sections 175(2) and (7) and 176 do not apply.
-- src:2864 | (4B) Where regulations are made by the Scottish Ministers under this section—
-- src:2865 | (a) sections 175(2) and (7) and 176 do not apply, and
@ref s 138(4B)(a) (src:2864-2865)
GIVEN `the regulations are made by the Scottish Ministers under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(4B)(a) sections 175(2) and (7) and 176 apply to the regulations` MEANS
    IF `the regulations are made by the Scottish Ministers under this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sections 175(2) and (7) and 176 do not apply"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where regulations are made by the Scottish Ministers under this section"

§§ `s 138(5) -- the three payments of paragraph (1)(b)`

-- "and any reference in this subsection to meeting a need or defraying an expense includes a reference to
-- helping to meet the need or to defray the expense."
-- src:2872 | and any reference in this subsection to meeting a need or defraying an expense includes a reference to helping to meet the need or to defray the expense.
@ref s 138(5) (src:2872)
GIVEN `the payment wholly meets the need or defrays the expense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment helps to meet the need or to defray the expense` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 138(5) the payment meets a need or defrays an expense` MEANS
    `the payment wholly meets the need or defrays the expense` OR `the payment helps to meet the need or to defray the expense`

-- src:2869 | “budgeting loan” means a loan awarded in circumstances specified in directions issued by the Secretary of State for the purpose of defraying an intermittent expense;
@ref s 138(5) “budgeting loan” (src:2869)
GIVEN `it is a loan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is awarded in circumstances specified in directions issued by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 138(5) the payment meets a need or defrays an expense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expense is an intermittent expense` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(5) the payment is a budgeting loan` MEANS
    IF     `it is a loan`
       AND `it is awarded in circumstances specified in directions issued by the Secretary of State`
       AND `s 138(5) the payment meets a need or defrays an expense`
       AND `the expense is an intermittent expense`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“budgeting loan” means a loan awarded in circumstances specified in directions ... for the purpose of defraying an intermittent expense"

-- src:2870 | “community care grant” means a grant awarded in circumstances so specified for the purpose of meeting a need for community care;
@ref s 138(5) “community care grant” (src:2870)
GIVEN `it is a grant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is awarded in circumstances specified in directions issued by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 138(5) the payment meets a need or defrays an expense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the need is a need for community care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(5) the payment is a community care grant` MEANS
    IF     `it is a grant`
       AND `it is awarded in circumstances specified in directions issued by the Secretary of State`
       AND `s 138(5) the payment meets a need or defrays an expense`
       AND `the need is a need for community care`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“community care grant” means a grant awarded in circumstances so specified for the purpose of meeting a need for community care"

-- src:2871 | “crisis loan” means a loan awarded in circumstances so specified for the purpose of meeting an immediate short term need;
@ref s 138(5) “crisis loan” (src:2871)
GIVEN `it is a loan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is awarded in circumstances specified in directions issued by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 138(5) the payment meets a need or defrays an expense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the need is an immediate short term need` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(5) the payment is a crisis loan` MEANS
    IF     `it is a loan`
       AND `it is awarded in circumstances specified in directions issued by the Secretary of State`
       AND `s 138(5) the payment meets a need or defrays an expense`
       AND `the need is an immediate short term need`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“crisis loan” means a loan awarded in circumstances so specified for the purpose of meeting an immediate short term need"

§§ `s 139 -- awards by social fund officers`

-- "an appropriate officer, that is to say, an officer of the Secretary of State who, acting under his authority,
-- is exercising functions of the Secretary of State in relation to payments so mentioned": "that is to say"
-- is read as a definition by "means" (decision P4).
-- src:2874 | (1) Whether a payment mentioned in section 138(1)(b) above is to be awarded, and how much it is to be, shall be determined by an appropriate officer, that is to say, an officer of the Secretary of State who, acting under his authority, is exercising functions of the Secretary of State in relation to payments so mentioned.
@ref s 139(1) (src:2874)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is acting under the authority of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exercising functions of the Secretary of State in relation to payments mentioned in section 138(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(1) the person is an appropriate officer` MEANS
    IF     `the person is an officer of the Secretary of State`
       AND `the person is acting under the authority of the Secretary of State`
       AND `the person is exercising functions of the Secretary of State in relation to payments mentioned in section 138(1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that is to say, an officer of the Secretary of State who, acting under his authority, is exercising functions of the Secretary of State in relation to payments so mentioned"

-- Whether a payment mentioned in section 138(1)(b) is to be awarded, and how much, is determined by an
-- appropriate officer.
-- src:2874 | (1) Whether a payment mentioned in section 138(1)(b) above is to be awarded, and how much it is to be, shall be determined by an appropriate officer, that is to say, an officer of the Secretary of State who, acting under his authority, is exercising functions of the Secretary of State in relation to payments so mentioned.
@ref s 139(1) (src:2874)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 138(1) Kind of payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(1) the question of whether to award and how much is one for an appropriate officer` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a community care grant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a crisis loan` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a budgeting loan` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet maternity expenses` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a payment mentioned in section 138(1)(b)"
    WHEN `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet funeral expenses` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a payment mentioned in section 138(1)(b)"
    WHEN `s 138(1) some other kind of payment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a payment mentioned in section 138(1)(b)"

-- A power: an appropriate officer may determine that an award is payable in instalments.
-- src:2875 | (2) An appropriate officer may determine that an award shall be payable in specified instalments at specified times.
@ref s 139(2) (src:2875)
GIVEN `s 139(1) the person is an appropriate officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(2) the person may determine that an award shall be payable in specified instalments at specified times` MEANS
    `s 124(1) holds or else nothing` `s 139(1) the person is an appropriate officer`   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appropriate officer may determine"

DECLARE `s 139 Party` IS ONE OF
    `s 139 the person by or on behalf of whom the application for the loan was made`

DECLARE `s 139 Duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 139 repay the loan on the terms the Secretary of State notified`

-- A crisis loan or budgeting loan is repayable on the terms the Secretary of State notified before payment.
-- Written twice: as a regulative rule (run with #TRACE) and as a decision function (which can be asserted).
-- src:2877 | (4) An award of a crisis loan or a budgeting loan shall be repayable upon such terms and conditions as before the award is paid the Secretary of State notifies to the person by or on behalf of whom the application for it was made.
@ref s 139(4) (src:2877)
`s 139(4) the duty to repay a crisis loan or budgeting loan on the notified terms` MEANS
    PARTY `s 139 the person by or on behalf of whom the application for the loan was made`
    MUST `s 139 repay the loan on the terms the Secretary of State notified`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 139 the person by or on behalf of whom the application for the loan was made` BECAUSE "the loan was not repaid upon the terms and conditions that the Secretary of State notified before the award was paid"

-- src:2877 | (4) An award of a crisis loan or a budgeting loan shall be repayable upon such terms and conditions as before the award is paid the Secretary of State notifies to the person by or on behalf of whom the application for it was made.
@ref s 139(4) (src:2877)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 138(1) Kind of payment`
      `before the award was paid the Secretary of State notified terms and conditions to the person by or on behalf of whom the application was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(4) the award is repayable on the notified terms` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a crisis loan` THEN
        IF `before the award was paid the Secretary of State notified terms and conditions to the person by or on behalf of whom the application was made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon such terms and conditions as before the award is paid the Secretary of State notifies"
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a budgeting loan` THEN
        IF `before the award was paid the Secretary of State notified terms and conditions to the person by or on behalf of whom the application was made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): same
    WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a community care grant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An award of a crisis loan or a budgeting loan"
    WHEN `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet maternity expenses` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): same
    WHEN `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet funeral expenses` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): same
    WHEN `s 138(1) some other kind of payment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): same

-- Payment of an award is made to the applicant unless the appropriate officer determines otherwise.
-- src:2878 | (5) Payment of an award shall be made to the applicant unless the appropriate officer determines otherwise.
@ref s 139(5) (src:2878)
GIVEN `the appropriate officer has determined that the payment is to be made otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(5) payment of the award is to be made to the applicant` MEANS
    IF `the appropriate officer has determined that the payment is to be made otherwise`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Payment of an award shall be made to the applicant unless the appropriate officer determines otherwise" -- the officer has determined otherwise
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 140 -- principles of determination`

DECLARE `s 140 Matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 140(1)(a) the nature, extent and urgency of the need`
    `s 140(1)(b) the existence of resources from which the need may be met`
    `s 140(1)(c) the possibility that some other person or body may wholly or partly meet it`
    `s 140(1)(d) where the payment is repayable, the likelihood of repayment and the time within which repayment is likely`
    `s 140(1)(e) any relevant allocation under section 168(1) to (4) of the Administration Act`
    `s 140(1) any other of the circumstances of the case`
    `s 140(1A)(a) such of the applicant's personal circumstances as are of a description specified in directions`

-- (1): for a community care grant or crisis loan, all the circumstances and in particular (a) to (e).
-- (1A): for a budgeting loan, the personal circumstances so specified and the criteria in (1)(b), (d) and (e).
-- Both are "subject to subsection (2)": a direction or guidance under (2) may displace the duty.
-- A matter that (1A) does not list, for a budgeting loan, is NOTHING: neither required nor excluded (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2880 | (1) In determining whether to make an award of a community care grant or a crisis loan to the applicant or the amount or value to be awarded an appropriate officer shall have regard, subject to subsection (2) below, to all the circumstances of the case and, in particular—
-- src:2881 | (a) the nature, extent and urgency of the need;
-- src:2882 | (b) the existence of resources from which the need may be met;
-- src:2883 | (c) the possibility that some other person or body may wholly or partly meet it;
-- src:2884 | (d) where the payment is repayable, the likelihood of repayment and the time within which repayment is likely;
-- src:2885 | (e) any relevant allocation under section 168(1) to (4) of the Administration Act.
@ref s 140(1) (src:2880-2885)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 138(1) Kind of payment`
      matter IS A `s 140 Matter`
      `the payment is repayable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction or guidance under subsection (2) displaces the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(1) the officer must have regard to the matter` MEANS
    IF `a direction or guidance under subsection (2) displaces the duty`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to subsection (2) below"
    ELSE
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a community care grant` THEN `s 140(1) the matter for a grant or a crisis loan` matter `the payment is repayable`
        WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a crisis loan` THEN `s 140(1) the matter for a grant or a crisis loan` matter `the payment is repayable`
        WHEN `s 138(1)(b) a budgeting loan` THEN `s 140(1A) the matter for a budgeting loan` matter `the payment is repayable`
        WHEN `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet maternity expenses` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for community care grants, crisis loans and budgeting loans
        WHEN `s 138(1)(a) a payment to meet funeral expenses` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): same
        WHEN `s 138(1) some other kind of payment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): same

-- src:2880 | (1) In determining whether to make an award of a community care grant or a crisis loan to the applicant or the amount or value to be awarded an appropriate officer shall have regard, subject to subsection (2) below, to all the circumstances of the case and, in particular—
-- src:2881 | (a) the nature, extent and urgency of the need;
-- src:2882 | (b) the existence of resources from which the need may be met;
-- src:2883 | (c) the possibility that some other person or body may wholly or partly meet it;
-- src:2884 | (d) where the payment is repayable, the likelihood of repayment and the time within which repayment is likely;
-- src:2885 | (e) any relevant allocation under section 168(1) to (4) of the Administration Act.
@ref s 140(1) (src:2880-2885)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 140 Matter`
      `the payment is repayable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(1) the matter for a grant or a crisis loan` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 140(1)(a) the nature, extent and urgency of the need` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 140(1)(b) the existence of resources from which the need may be met` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 140(1)(c) the possibility that some other person or body may wholly or partly meet it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 140(1)(d) where the payment is repayable, the likelihood of repayment and the time within which repayment is likely` THEN
        IF `the payment is repayable` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the payment is repayable"
    WHEN `s 140(1)(e) any relevant allocation under section 168(1) to (4) of the Administration Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 140(1) any other of the circumstances of the case` THEN JUST TRUE   -- "all the circumstances of the case"
    WHEN `s 140(1A)(a) such of the applicant's personal circumstances as are of a description specified in directions` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1) does not name it, but "all the circumstances" is wide enough that this is a gloss, not a refusal

-- src:2886 | (1A) Subject to subsection (2) below, in determining whether to make an award of a budgeting loan to the applicant, or the amount or value to be awarded, an appropriate officer shall have regard to—
-- src:2887 | (a) such of the applicant’s personal circumstances as are of a description specified in directions issued by the Secretary of State; and
-- src:2888 | (b) the criteria specified in paragraphs (b), (d) and (e) of subsection (1) above;
@ref s 140(1A) (src:2886-2888)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 140 Matter`
      `the payment is repayable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(1A) the matter for a budgeting loan` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 140(1A)(a) such of the applicant's personal circumstances as are of a description specified in directions` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 140(1)(b) the existence of resources from which the need may be met` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 140(1)(d) where the payment is repayable, the likelihood of repayment and the time within which repayment is likely` THEN
        IF `the payment is repayable` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the criteria specified in paragraphs (b), (d) and (e)", and (d) is for "where the payment is repayable"
    WHEN `s 140(1)(e) any relevant allocation under section 168(1) to (4) of the Administration Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 140(1)(a) the nature, extent and urgency of the need` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b), (d) and (e)" are the criteria named
    WHEN `s 140(1)(c) the possibility that some other person or body may wholly or partly meet it` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): same
    WHEN `s 140(1) any other of the circumstances of the case` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1A) lists the matters and does not say "all the circumstances"

DECLARE `s 140 Party` IS ONE OF
    `s 140 an appropriate officer`

DECLARE `s 140 Duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 140 have regard to the matters the section requires`
    `s 140 determine in accordance with the general directions and take account of the general guidance`
    `s 140 take account of the guidance of the officer nominated for the area`

-- src:2880 | (1) In determining whether to make an award of a community care grant or a crisis loan to the applicant or the amount or value to be awarded an appropriate officer shall have regard, subject to subsection (2) below, to all the circumstances of the case and, in particular—
-- src:2881 | (a) the nature, extent and urgency of the need;
-- src:2882 | (b) the existence of resources from which the need may be met;
-- src:2883 | (c) the possibility that some other person or body may wholly or partly meet it;
-- src:2884 | (d) where the payment is repayable, the likelihood of repayment and the time within which repayment is likely;
-- src:2885 | (e) any relevant allocation under section 168(1) to (4) of the Administration Act.
@ref s 140(1) (src:2880-2885)
`s 140(1) the appropriate officer's duty to have regard` MEANS
    PARTY `s 140 an appropriate officer`
    MUST `s 140 have regard to the matters the section requires`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 140 an appropriate officer` BECAUSE "in determining whether to make an award and how much, the appropriate officer did not have regard to the matters section 140(1) or (1A) requires"

-- (2): the officer determines any question in accordance with general directions and takes account of general guidance.
-- src:2890 | (2) An appropriate officer shall determine any question in accordance with any general directions issued by the Secretary of State and in determining any question shall take account of any general guidance issued by him.
@ref s 140(2) (src:2890)
`s 140(2) the appropriate officer's duty to follow the general directions` MEANS
    PARTY `s 140 an appropriate officer`
    MUST `s 140 determine in accordance with the general directions and take account of the general guidance`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 140 an appropriate officer` BECAUSE "the appropriate officer did not determine the question in accordance with the general directions issued by the Secretary of State, or did not take account of the general guidance issued by him"

-- src:2890 | (2) An appropriate officer shall determine any question in accordance with any general directions issued by the Secretary of State and in determining any question shall take account of any general guidance issued by him.
@ref s 140(2) (src:2890)
GIVEN `the determination is in accordance with every general direction issued by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has taken account of any general guidance issued by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(2) the officer has done what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the determination is in accordance with every general direction issued by the Secretary of State` AND `the officer has taken account of any general guidance issued by the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the duty's own content): "shall determine any question in accordance with any general directions ... and ... shall take account of any general guidance"

-- (4ZA): a direction under (4)(da) may fix the sum by applying a multiplier to the most recent relevant sum.
-- src:2904 | (4ZA) A direction under subsection (4)(da) may require the sum to be determined by applying, or by a method that includes applying, a multiplier specified in the direction in circumstances specified in the direction to the most recent relevant sum published by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 140(4ZA) (src:2904)
GIVEN `the multiplier specified in the direction` IS A NUMBER
      `the most recent relevant sum published by the Secretary of State in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 140(4ZA) the sum determined by applying the multiplier in pounds` MEANS
    `the multiplier specified in the direction` TIMES `the most recent relevant sum published by the Secretary of State in pounds`

DECLARE `s 140(4ZB) Defined term` IS ONE OF
    `s 140(4ZB) relevant sum`

-- src:2905 | (4ZB) A relevant sum is a sum determined from time to time by reference to so much of any relevant allocation under section 168(1) to (4) of the Administration Act as is available for making payments.
@ref s 140(4ZB) (src:2905)
GIVEN term IS A `s 140(4ZB) Defined term`
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 140(4ZB) how the term is defined` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a plain statement of what the term is`
        `what it points at or says` IS "a sum determined from time to time by reference to so much of any relevant allocation under section 168(1) to (4) of the Administration Act as is available for making payments"

-- (5): take account of the guidance of the officer nominated for his area, subject to the Secretary of State's directions or guidance.
-- src:2906 | (5) In determining a question an appropriate officer shall take account (subject to any directions or guidance issued by the Secretary of State under this section) of any guidance issued by the appropriate officer nominated for his area under section 36 of the Social Security Act 1998.
@ref s 140(5) (src:2906)
GIVEN `a direction or guidance issued by the Secretary of State under this section displaces it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(5) the officer must take account of the guidance of the officer nominated for the area` MEANS
    IF `a direction or guidance issued by the Secretary of State under this section displaces it`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any directions or guidance issued by the Secretary of State under this section"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Part 8A -- Health in pregnancy grant (ss 140A-140B)`

§§ `s 140A -- entitlement`

-- "woman" means a female of any age.  The core's Sex is the sex a witness would state; Woman is "female".
-- src:2918 | “woman” means a female of any age.
@ref s 140A(5) “woman” (src:2918)
GIVEN sex IS A Sex
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140A(5) the person is a woman` MEANS
    CONSIDER sex
    WHEN Woman THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN Man THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“woman” means a female of any age"

DECLARE `s 140A(5) Defined term` IS ONE OF
    `s 140A(5) health professional`
    `s 140A(5) prescribed`
    `s 140A(5) woman`

-- The three definitions as the Act words them: the first two borrow their content from regulations.
-- src:2916 | “health professional” has such meaning as may be prescribed,
-- src:2917 | “prescribed” means prescribed by regulations, and
-- src:2918 | “woman” means a female of any age.
@ref s 140A(5) (src:2916-2918)
GIVEN term IS A `s 140A(5) Defined term`
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 140A(5) how the term is defined` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `s 140A(5) health professional` THEN
        `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
            `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
            `what it points at or says` IS "such meaning as may be prescribed"
    WHEN `s 140A(5) prescribed` THEN
        `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
            `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
            `what it points at or says` IS "prescribed by regulations"
    WHEN `s 140A(5) woman` THEN
        `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
            `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
            `what it points at or says` IS "a female of any age"

-- (1): a woman who satisfies prescribed conditions in relation to a pregnancy of hers is entitled to a lump sum.
-- src:2909 | (1) A woman who satisfies prescribed conditions in relation to a pregnancy of hers is entitled to payment of a lump sum (to be known as “health in pregnancy grant”).
@ref s 140A(1) (src:2909)
GIVEN `s 140A(5) the person is a woman` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `she satisfies prescribed conditions in relation to a pregnancy of hers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140A(1) the woman is entitled to payment of health in pregnancy grant` MEANS
    `s 124(1) holds or else nothing` (`s 124(1) both hold` `s 140A(5) the person is a woman` (JUST `she satisfies prescribed conditions in relation to a pregnancy of hers`))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A woman who satisfies prescribed conditions"

-- (2): not entitled unless she reached the 25th week of her pregnancy before 1 January 2011.
-- src:2910 | (2) A woman is not entitled to health in pregnancy grant unless she has reached the 25th week of her pregnancy before 1st January 2011.
@ref s 140A(2) (src:2910)
GIVEN `she has reached the 25th week of her pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which she reached the 25th week of her pregnancy` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140A(2) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as subsection (2) goes` MEANS
    IF `she has reached the 25th week of her pregnancy` AND `the date on which she reached the 25th week of her pregnancy` LESS THAN Date 1 1 2011
    THEN JUST TRUE    -- the subsection's "unless" is met, so it bars nothing; the function is named "as far as subsection (2) goes", so it says nothing of entitlement under the rest of s 140A
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A woman is not entitled to health in pregnancy grant unless she has reached the 25th week of her pregnancy before 1st January 2011"

-- (3)(a): not entitled unless she has received advice on matters relating to maternal health from a health professional.
-- src:2911 | (3) A woman is not entitled to health in pregnancy grant unless—
-- src:2912 | (a) she has received advice on matters relating to maternal health from a health professional;
@ref s 140A(3)(a) (src:2911-2912)
GIVEN `she has received advice on matters relating to maternal health from a health professional` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140A(3)(a) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as paragraph (a) goes` MEANS
    IF `she has received advice on matters relating to maternal health from a health professional`
    THEN JUST TRUE    -- the paragraph's "unless" is met, so it bars nothing: as far as paragraph (a) goes
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A woman is not entitled to health in pregnancy grant unless— (a) she has received advice on matters relating to maternal health from a health professional"

-- (3)(b): not entitled unless she is in Great Britain at the time she claims (or is treated, under (4), as being there).
-- src:2911 | (3) A woman is not entitled to health in pregnancy grant unless—
-- src:2912 | (a) she has received advice on matters relating to maternal health from a health professional;
-- src:2913 | (b) she is in Great Britain at the time she makes a claim for the grant in accordance with the Administration Act.
@ref s 140A(3)(b) (src:2911-2913)
GIVEN `she is in Great Britain at the time she makes a claim for the grant in accordance with the Administration Act (or is treated, under regulations, as being there)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140A(3)(b) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as paragraph (b) goes` MEANS
    IF `she is in Great Britain at the time she makes a claim for the grant in accordance with the Administration Act (or is treated, under regulations, as being there)`
    THEN JUST TRUE    -- the paragraph's "unless" is met, so it bars nothing: as far as paragraph (b) goes
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A woman is not entitled to health in pregnancy grant unless— ... (b) she is in Great Britain at the time she makes a claim"

-- The grant and the three bars together.  A bar the Act states beats the grant; otherwise the grant's own answer stands.
-- src:2909 | (1) A woman who satisfies prescribed conditions in relation to a pregnancy of hers is entitled to payment of a lump sum (to be known as “health in pregnancy grant”).
-- src:2910 | (2) A woman is not entitled to health in pregnancy grant unless she has reached the 25th week of her pregnancy before 1st January 2011.
-- src:2911 | (3) A woman is not entitled to health in pregnancy grant unless—
-- src:2912 | (a) she has received advice on matters relating to maternal health from a health professional;
-- src:2913 | (b) she is in Great Britain at the time she makes a claim for the grant in accordance with the Administration Act.
@ref s 140A(1) (src:2909-2913)
GIVEN `s 140A(1) the woman is entitled to payment of health in pregnancy grant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 140A(2) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as subsection (2) goes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 140A(3)(a) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as paragraph (a) goes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 140A(3)(b) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as paragraph (b) goes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140A the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 124(1) all of these hold` (LIST
                  `s 140A(2) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as subsection (2) goes`
                  , `s 140A(3)(a) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as paragraph (a) goes`
                  , `s 140A(3)(b) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as paragraph (b) goes`)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 140A(1) the woman is entitled to payment of health in pregnancy grant`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 140A(1) the woman is entitled to payment of health in pregnancy grant`

§§ `s 140B -- amount`

-- The amount is whatever regulations of the Treasury prescribe; the Act states none.
-- src:2921 | (1) Health in pregnancy grant is to be of an amount prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury.
@ref s 140B(1) (src:2921)
GIVEN `the amount prescribed for the case, if there is one, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 140B(1) the amount of health in pregnancy grant in pounds` MEANS
    `the amount prescribed for the case, if there is one, in pounds`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when none is given: "of an amount prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury"
